cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Foretec EnergyBench, its code or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Foretec EnergyBench: a live, gate-aligned benchmark of day-ahead forecasts for European power markets"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Genov
    given-names: Evgenii
    affiliation: "Foretec; Vrije Universiteit Brussel"
    email: evgeny@foretec.be
url: "https://energybench.foretec.co"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ujohn33/foretec-energy-bench"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.57967/hf/11052"
    description: "The dataset (every forecast, actual and score) on Hugging Face"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - energy forecasting
  - electricity price forecasting
  - wind power forecasting
  - solar power forecasting
  - load forecasting
  - time series foundation models
  - benchmark
  - day-ahead market
abstract: >-
  An open, live benchmark for day-ahead electricity forecasting. Every day before the 12:00 day-ahead auction gate,
  every model forecasts each quarter-hour of the next delivery day for price, wind, solar and load in BE, NL, FR,
  DE-LU, DK1 and DK2 from one frozen set of public inputs (history, numerical weather predictions, the ENTSO-E load
  forecast, fuel prices), and is scored against the grid operators' actuals. Code under Apache-2.0; the published
  forecasts and scores under CC BY 4.0.
